<mxfile host="Electron" agent="most-exchange" compressed="false">
  <diagram name="System Architecture" id="most-architecture">
    <mxGraphModel dx="2793" dy="1421" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1169" pageHeight="827" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" parent="1" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=24;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1F2933;" value="most-exchange — system architecture" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="34" width="900" x="40" y="16" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="subtitle" parent="1" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=13;fontColor=#5A6570;" value="One shard shown in full. Books are independent, so capacity is added by adding shards — never more securities per shard (max 10 per shard, 1M orders per book). Gateways are a &lt;b&gt;separate tier&lt;/b&gt;: they hold no state, so their number and placement are a deployment choice rather than a design constraint." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="34" width="1360" x="40" y="48" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="upstream" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F4F4F4;strokeColor=#9AA0A6;dashed=1;fontSize=13;fontColor=#4A5560;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" value="&lt;b&gt;Upstream protocol gateways&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;— FIX, proprietary session protocols.&lt;br&gt;They translate their own wire format to the SBE of §5, embed &lt;b&gt;DirectoryClient&lt;/b&gt; to route by security, and are &lt;b&gt;partitioned across the gateways below&lt;/b&gt;." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="62" width="1360" x="40" y="100" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gwtier" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FAFBFC;strokeColor=#8FA8C8;verticalAlign=top;align=center;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=4;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#2C3E50;container=1;collapsible=0;arcSize=12;" value="GATEWAY TIER — stateless, any number, and &lt;i&gt;not&lt;/i&gt; co-located with the cluster nodes" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="220" width="1360" x="40" y="216" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gwa" parent="gwtier" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#D5E8D4;strokeColor=#82B366;fontSize=12;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" value="&lt;b&gt;gateway&lt;/b&gt; · gw-a&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;validates securityId against the shard map&lt;br&gt;authenticates to the cluster as &lt;b&gt;gw-a&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;sends cluster keepalives (1s)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;its own&lt;/i&gt; client in 20 · client out 21" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="420" x="24" y="52" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gwb" parent="gwtier" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#D5E8D4;strokeColor=#82B366;fontSize=12;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" value="&lt;b&gt;gateway&lt;/b&gt; · gw-b&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;same binary, same shard, &lt;b&gt;disjoint endpoints&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;authenticates as &lt;b&gt;gw-b&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;its own&lt;/i&gt; client in 40 · client out 41" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="420" x="464" y="52" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gwmore" parent="gwtier" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#EEF6EC;strokeColor=#82B366;dashed=1;fontSize=12;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontColor=#3F6B33;" value="&lt;b&gt;gw-c …&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:11px;&quot;&gt;one per adapter group;&lt;br&gt;losing one costs its&lt;br&gt;adapters a reconnect&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="160" x="904" y="52" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gwstate" parent="gwtier" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFDE7;strokeColor=#D6B656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;fontColor=#4A4A4A;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;No per-order state.&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;Stated by the &lt;b&gt;engine&lt;/b&gt; on every report, so a replacement reports correctly on orders it never saw.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Never share an inbound channel.&lt;/b&gt; Two gateways subscribed to one would each receive every order and forward both — duplicate orders, not redundancy. What is disjoint is endpoints, not state.&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="252" x="1084" y="52" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="shard0" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FAFBFC;strokeColor=#8FA8C8;verticalAlign=top;align=center;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=4;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#2C3E50;container=1;collapsible=0;" value="SHARD 0 — one security list, one fingerprint (ShardSpec.fingerprint), printed by every process in this box" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="430" width="1360" x="40" y="478" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cluster0" parent="shard0" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#EAF1FB;strokeColor=#6C8EBF;verticalAlign=top;align=center;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=4;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1F4E79;container=1;collapsible=0;" value="Aeron Cluster — Raft-replicated log, 3 or 5 nodes. &lt;i&gt;One machine per node.&lt;/i&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="310" width="780" x="24" y="56" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="node0" parent="cluster0" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#6C8EBF;verticalAlign=top;align=center;spacingTop=2;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1F4E79;container=1;collapsible=0;" value="Node 0 — LEADER" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="236" width="240" x="16" y="56" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="drv0" parent="node0" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#EDEDED;strokeColor=#9AA0A6;fontSize=11;align=center;" value="ClusteredMediaDriver&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;media driver + archive&lt;br&gt;+ consensus module · &lt;b&gt;authenticates gateways&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;allocates — own process&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="88" width="208" x="16" y="34" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eng0" parent="node0" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#DAE8FC;strokeColor=#6C8EBF;fontSize=11;align=center;" value="&lt;b&gt;engine&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;MatchingEngineService&lt;br&gt;single-threaded, deterministic, no clock&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;holds origQty&lt;/b&gt; in the cold word&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="88" width="208" x="16" y="134" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="node1" parent="cluster0" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#6C8EBF;verticalAlign=top;align=center;spacingTop=2;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1F4E79;container=1;collapsible=0;" value="Node 1 — follower" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="236" width="240" x="272" y="56" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="drv1" parent="node1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#EDEDED;strokeColor=#9AA0A6;fontSize=11;align=center;" value="ClusteredMediaDriver&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;+ market-data + discovery&lt;br&gt;run here too&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="88" width="208" x="16" y="34" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eng1" parent="node1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#DAE8FC;strokeColor=#6C8EBF;fontSize=11;align=center;" value="&lt;b&gt;engine&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;identical service over&lt;br&gt;the identical log —&lt;br&gt;byte-identical state&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="88" width="208" x="16" y="134" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="node2" parent="cluster0" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#6C8EBF;verticalAlign=top;align=center;spacingTop=2;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1F4E79;container=1;collapsible=0;" value="Node 2 — follower" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="236" width="240" x="528" y="56" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="drv2" parent="node2" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#EDEDED;strokeColor=#9AA0A6;fontSize=11;align=center;" value="ClusteredMediaDriver" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="88" width="208" x="16" y="34" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eng2" parent="node2" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#DAE8FC;strokeColor=#6C8EBF;fontSize=11;align=center;" value="&lt;b&gt;engine&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 10px;&quot;&gt;a crash here kills&lt;br&gt;every node at the&lt;br&gt;same log position&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="88" width="208" x="16" y="134" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="mds0" parent="shard0" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E1D5E7;strokeColor=#9673A6;fontSize=12;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" value="&lt;b&gt;market-data&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;derives L1 / L2 / L3 from&lt;br&gt;the book event stream&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:11px;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;runs on every node; a follower’s is subscribed to a silent stream, so failover needs no standby logic&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="210" width="250" x="850" y="56" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="regnote" parent="shard0" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFDE7;strokeColor=#D6B656;align=center;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;fontColor=#4A4A4A;" value="&lt;b&gt;Participant registry&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px;&quot;&gt;Published per shard.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The consensus module authenticates a connecting gateway against it and stamps the gateway id on the session as the encoded principal. The engine turns that principal back into a participant list and binds every one at session open.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Both re-read it in place&lt;/b&gt; — every 5s, compared by content fingerprint — so changing who speaks for whom restarts a &lt;i&gt;gateway&lt;/i&gt;, never a node.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Legal because the map it feeds is node-local egress routing, not replicated state.&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="258" width="220" x="1120" y="56" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="shardnote" parent="shard0" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=11;fontColor=#5A6570;" value="Every process here boots from the &lt;b&gt;same&lt;/b&gt; shard security file and prints the same fingerprint. A mismatch would diverge the books rather than fail loudly —&lt;br&gt;the one class of misconfiguration consensus cannot catch. The participant registry has its &lt;b&gt;own&lt;/b&gt; fingerprint: rotating a secret is not a change of geometry." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="44" width="1050" x="50" y="372" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e5" edge="1" parent="shard0" source="cluster0" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#9673A6;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;exitX=1;exitY=0.835;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;exitPerimeter=0;entryX=0.12;entryY=1;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" value="Book Event Stream&lt;br&gt;IPC 12 · &lt;i&gt;leader only&lt;/i&gt;" target="mds0">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" x="0.1029" y="-20" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint as="offset" />
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="804" y="312" />
              <mxPoint x="880" y="312" />
              <mxPoint x="880" y="266" />
            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="shardN" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FAFBFC;strokeColor=#8FA8C8;dashed=1;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontColor=#2C3E50;" value="&lt;b&gt;SHARD 1 … SHARD N&lt;/b&gt; — identical topology: its own cluster, security list and fingerprint.&lt;br&gt;Books are fully independent (no cross-instrument matching). Feed sequences are namespaced by shardId, so several shards can share one multicast group." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="80" width="1360" x="40" y="920" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="l1" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFE6CC;strokeColor=#D79B00;fontSize=12;align=center;" value="&lt;b&gt;L1&lt;/b&gt; · TopOfBook + LastTrade&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px;&quot;&gt;239.10.1.1:40001 · stream 1&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="72" width="430" x="40" y="1032" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="l2" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFE6CC;strokeColor=#D79B00;fontSize=12;align=center;" value="&lt;b&gt;L2&lt;/b&gt; · DepthUpdate + snapshot cycle&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px;&quot;&gt;239.10.1.2:40002 · stream 2&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="72" width="430" x="485" y="1032" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="l3" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFE6CC;strokeColor=#D79B00;fontSize=12;align=center;" value="&lt;b&gt;L3&lt;/b&gt; · book events, forwarded verbatim&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px;&quot;&gt;239.10.1.3:40003 · stream 3 · &lt;b&gt;the only feed carrying VolatilityHalted&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="72" width="470" x="930" y="1032" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="feednote" parent="1" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=11;fontColor=#5A6570;" value="SBE over UDP multicast, &lt;b&gt;MaxMulticastFlowControl&lt;/b&gt; — the fastest receiver governs, so a slow subscriber takes an unrecoverable gap rather than throttling the publisher. Gap detection and re-synchronisation are the subscriber’s job (FeedSequenceTracker, DepthFeedAssembler)." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="26" width="1360" x="40" y="1110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="downstream" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F4F4F4;strokeColor=#9AA0A6;dashed=1;fontSize=13;fontColor=#4A5560;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" value="&lt;b&gt;Market data adapters&lt;/b&gt; — Embed DirectoryClient to map securityId → symbol, and DepthFeedAssembler to splice snapshots onto increments." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="60" width="1360" x="40" y="1144" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cp" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F2FBFB;strokeColor=#0E8088;verticalAlign=top;align=center;spacingLeft=14;spacingTop=4;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#0E5F63;container=1;collapsible=0;" value="CONTROL PLANE — authors reference data, drives the trading day. Never on any process’s boot path. &lt;i&gt;Runs in Kubernetes.&lt;/i&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="372" width="1030" x="1510" y="96" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="vue" parent="cp" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#0E8088;fontSize=12;align=center;" value="&lt;b&gt;Admin frontend (Vue)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px;&quot;&gt;shards · securities · participants&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;gateways&lt;/b&gt; · releases · schedules&lt;br&gt;operations · live books&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="86" width="290" x="30" y="52" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cli" parent="cp" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#0E8088;fontSize=12;align=center;" value="&lt;b&gt;most&lt;/b&gt; — operator CLI&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px;&quot;&gt;securities · send · cancel · book&lt;br&gt;define · session · purge · image&lt;br&gt;cluster · load&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="86" width="290" x="350" y="52" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pg" parent="cp" style="shape=cylinder3;boundedLbl=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=12;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#D6B656;fontSize=12;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" value="&lt;b&gt;PostgreSQL&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px;&quot;&gt;shards · securities · participants&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;gateways&lt;/b&gt; · schedules · holidays&lt;br&gt;releases · operators · audit&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="86" width="290" x="670" y="52" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ctl" parent="cp" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#B0E3E6;strokeColor=#0E8088;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" value="&lt;b&gt;control&lt;/b&gt; — Spring Boot&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:11px;&quot;&gt;authenticated REST · publishes immutable releases · Aeron client for operator commands · watches discovery + L3 · scheduler · operator audit&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Reference data is validated by constructing the real&lt;/i&gt; reference &lt;i&gt;domain types — the fingerprint and the registry are never reimplemented here.&lt;br&gt;Each scheduler tick reconciles the phase the calendar wants against the phase L3 reports, and sends the difference.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="930" x="30" y="186" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e13" edge="1" parent="cp" source="vue" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#0E8088;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;dashed=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.156;entryY=-0.015;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;entryPerimeter=0;" target="ctl" value="REST">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points" />
            <mxPoint x="175" y="184" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e12" edge="1" parent="cp" source="pg" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#0E8088;fontSize=11;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;startArrow=block;startFill=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.843;entryY=0.001;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;entryPerimeter=0;" target="ctl" value="">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="814" y="138" />
            </Array>
            <mxPoint x="815" y="184" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rel" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#666666;dashed=1;fontSize=13;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" value="&lt;b&gt;Published release&lt;/b&gt; · releases/000007/ — immutable, never rewritten&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:11px;&quot;&gt;shard-N-securities.properties · &lt;b&gt;shard-N-participants.properties&lt;/b&gt; · discovery.properties&lt;br&gt;manifest.json — shard fingerprint &lt;i&gt;and&lt;/i&gt; registry fingerprint, per shard&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;These files, not the database, are what every process boots from. Put in force by moving a symlink.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="124" width="800" x="1740" y="516" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="disc" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFE6CC;strokeColor=#D79B00;fontSize=14;align=center;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=8;fontColor=#7A4F00;" value="&lt;b&gt;discovery&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:11px;&quot;&gt;Broadcasts the tradable universe on a repeating cycle — no request protocol, so a restarted adapter recovers on its own. Stateless, so running one per node is safe.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Publishes the &lt;b&gt;gateway’s&lt;/b&gt; client endpoints, not the cluster’s: an adapter that connected to the cluster would bypass securityId validation and the participant binding that decides where a maker’s fills go.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;One order-entry endpoint per shard — several gateways sit behind one virtual address until ShardEntry carries more.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;239.10.0.1:40000 · stream 100&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="370" width="340" x="1510" y="740" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notes" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFDE7;strokeColor=#D6B656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;fontSize=11;fontColor=#4A4A4A;" value="&lt;b&gt;Invariants this shape encodes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• A node is &lt;b&gt;two processes&lt;/b&gt;. The driver allocates, so it stays out of the engine.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• The engine never calls a clock for anything that reaches the log. Time is the sequenced consensus timestamp.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Book events and egress are &lt;b&gt;leader-only&lt;/b&gt;; the book event stream is muted on followers via onRoleChange.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Order state lives in the engine&lt;/b&gt;, in a cold word beside the one-cache-line order, a report carries orderQty, cumQty and leavesQty.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Operator commands take the &lt;b&gt;same path as an order&lt;/b&gt; and are sequenced through the log — there is no control channel.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Commands are &lt;b&gt;unacknowledged&lt;/b&gt;. SessionChanged on L3 confirms a phase; nothing confirms a SecurityDefinition.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• A halt is visible &lt;b&gt;only on L3&lt;/b&gt;, and recovery is operator-driven." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="320" width="430" x="2110" y="820" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
